# Frontend (macOS SwiftUI + TCA) — Overview

## Structure (Domain-based)

- **Cohesion**: Related functionality grouped by business domain
- **Separation**: Clear boundaries between domains
- **Dependencies**: Core infrastructure provides shared services
- **Scalability**: Easy to add new domains (e.g., AI/Search, Settings, etc.)

## Backend bootstrap from app

- **Swift-dotenv approach**: Environment variables loaded from `.env` at repo root
- **Implementation**: [BackendManagerDotenv.swift](mdc:apps/macos/Voyager/VoyagerHelper/BackendManagerDotenv.swift)
- **Environment keys**: `BACKEND_DIR`, `VOYAGER_PATH`, `VOYAGER_HOST`, `VOYAGER_PORT`, `BACKEND_URL`, `VOYAGER_LOG_FILE`
- **Backend execution modes**:
  - **Debug builds**: Uses local `uv` to launch backend (`uv run dev|prod`)
  - **Release builds**: Uses bundled `backend-venv/bin/python` from app resources
    - Venv prepared by [scripts/prepare-backend-venv.sh](mdc:scripts/prepare-backend-venv.sh) during build
    - Self-contained app bundle without requiring local `uv` installation

## Notes

- Prefer deriving API base from `BACKEND_URL`.
- Ensure helper launches backend before issuing API calls.
- See [12-frontend-http-client-guidelines.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/12-frontend-http-client-guidelines.mdc) for HTTP client patterns.
- See [13-frontend-tca-conventions.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/13-frontend-tca-conventions.mdc) for TCA conventions.
- See [11-frontend-dotenv-integration.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/11-frontend-dotenv-integration.mdc) for Swift-dotenv usage.
